  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Participatory budget monitoring with citizens&#x2019; groups in three districts</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Focusing on selected areas of Aileo, Liqui&#xe7;&#xe1; and Manatuto Districts, Mata Dalan Institute (MDI) seeks to empower ordinary East Timorese people to ensure the transparency and accountability of their governmental structures at both district and national levels, especially in respect of public service and public service delivery on health, education and old age pensions, and the Local Development Plans.  The activities include budget research and analysis, empowerment and awareness-raising, capacity-building for civil society organisations and citizens&#x2019; groups, participatory monitoring of government budgets and infrastructure development at district and national-level, and advocacy. MDI, which has a network of volunteers at district level, has shown particular success in providing young people with the opportunity to engage and make a positive contribution to East Timorese society.</narrative>
  </description>
